<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cyril of White Lake</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1337–1427</span> · Also known as Kirill Belozersky, Saint Cyril of Beloozero</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Cyril of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-beloye">White Lake</a> was a Russian monk and saint. A monk of the Simonov Monastery in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a>, he left in 1397 for the remote north, where he founded a monastery on the Siverskoye lake near Beloozero. He wrote a rule for its community and letters of advice to princes. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kirillo-belozersky-monastery">Kirillo-Belozersky Monastery</a> he founded became one of the richest in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>, and he was canonised in the 16th century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cyril-of-white-lake.jpg" alt="Cyril of White Lake" width="320" height="396" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kirill_Belozerskiy_icon_Dionisiy_Glushitskiy.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
